}},{"id":"T06","name":"System Persistence","shortDescription":{"text":"Installs cross-session backdoors, hooks, services, or scheduled tasks that survive the skill run"}},{"id":"T07","name":"Tool Hijacking and Spoofing","shortDescription":{"text":"Modifies, wraps, spoofs, or replaces tools so legitimate-looking calls execute attacker logic"}},{"id":"T08","name":"Insecure Dependencies","shortDescription":{"text":"Introduces malicious packages or components through dependency confusion, typosquatting, or unsafe sources"}},{"id":"T09","name":"Insecure Skill Coding Practices","shortDescription":{"text":"Exposes exploitable flaws such as hardcoded secrets, command injection, plaintext sensitive data, or unsafe temp files"}},{"id":"other","name":"Other Risk","shortDescription":{"text":"Security issues not covered by the T01-T09 classification"}}]}},"results":[{"ruleId":"T09","level":"warning","message":{"text":"Configuration normalization silently removes the operator's interception policy"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"bundled/openclaw-plugin/index.js"}}}],"partialFingerprints":{"primaryLocationLineHash":"f4667c1eb5adf9c9"},"properties":{"description":"### Impact\n\nThe configured approval gate is ineffective, including when the defence pipeline classifies content as BLOCK or QUARANTINE but the inline X-Ray guard does not reject it. This proves bypass of this plugin's approval layer, not successful persistence through any downstream server protections.","severity":"Medium"}},{"ruleId":"T09","level":"warning","message":{"text":"Default-on bootstrap repair deletes legacy directories and overwrites persistent hook files without confirmation"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"bundled/cortex-memory-hook/handler.ts"}}}],"partialFingerprints":{"primaryLocationLineHash":"823b3d3799fcfc7c"},"properties":{"description":"### Impact\n\nExisting legacy hook contents can be irreversibly removed, and canonical hook files can be replaced so subsequent gateway starts load the copied implementation. These are concrete destructive and persistent changes, not evidence of a hidden backdoor.","severity":"Medium"}}],"properties":{"securityScore":50,"primaryLanguage":"JavaScript","llm":"gpt-6.1-sol","startTime":1792480512.537284,"endTime":1792480627.5796447}}]},"skillspector":{"skill":{"name":"unknown","source":"/tmp/clawhub-codex-scan-v5762gr5sdpr1426w2qhec4b2n8gmbre-QrSxgt/clawscan-skillspector-4078761460/artifact","scanned_at":"2026-10-20T07:15:11.233745+00:00"},"risk_assessment":{"score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","max_issue_severity":"HIGH"},"components":[{"path":"SKILL.md","type":"markdown","lines":329,"executable":false,"size_bytes":32169,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"bundled/cortex-memory-hook/HOOK.md","type":"markdown","lines":177,"executable":false,"size_bytes":8053,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"bundled/cortex-memory-hook/handler.ts","type":"typescript","lines":1204,"executable":true,"size_bytes":47661,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"bundled/cortex-memory-hook/runtime.mjs","type":"other","lines":241,"executable":true,"size_bytes":9228,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"bundled/openclaw-plugin/cloud-sync.js","type":"javascript","lines":30,"executable":true,"size_bytes":1371,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"bundled/openclaw-plugin/index.js","type":"javascript","lines":709,"executable":true,"size_bytes":30414,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"bundled/openclaw-plugin/intercept-ingest.js","type":"javascript","lines":23,"executable":true,"size_bytes":936,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"bundled/openclaw-plugin/interceptor.js","type":"javascript","lines":346,"executable":true,"size_bytes":14883,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"bundled/openclaw-plugin/openclaw.plugin.json","type":"json","lines":205,"executable":false,"size_bytes":5788,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null}],"structured_summaries":[],"issues":[{"id":"AS1","finding_id":"finding-b08d693017944e779c0a6075573b7883","category":"Agent Snooping","pattern":"Agent Config Directory Access","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":53,"end_line":null,"start_column":32},"finding":"/.continue/config.json","explanation":"Skill reads from agent configuration directories (.claude/, .codex/, .gemini/). These directories may contain API keys, personal settings, and other credentials that the skill has no legitimate need to access.","remediation":"Remove all code or instructions that access agent configuration directories (.claude/, .codex/, .gemini/). If configuration values are needed, pass them explicitly as parameters or environment variables — never read the agent's own config files.","code_snippet":"    - $CWD/.claude/, $CWD/.cursor/ (project-level configs)\n    - $CWD/.cursorrules, $CWD/.windsurfrules, $CWD/.clinerules\n    - $CWD/CLAUDE.md, $CWD/copilot-instructions.md\n    - $CWD/.aider.conf.yml, $CWD/.continue/config.json\n    - $CWD/.env (env-scanner checks for leaked secrets — reads, never writes)\n  paths_write:\n    - ~/.shieldcortex/ (memory DB, config, cortex log, licence, audit cache)","intent":null,"tags":["Agent Snooping","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{"llm_review_outcome":"disagreed","llm_review_confidence":0.95},"match_fingerprint":"510c704042cfff5c23d8f21099c645b7a24494ea73f39ec042da2212277a2d16","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":53,"end_line":null,"start_column":32}]},{"id":"PE3","finding_id":"finding-e7af38e9706a4098abb2a13d640b518b","category":"Privilege Escalation","pattern":"Credential Access","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.6,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":54,"end_line":null,"start_column":11},"finding":".env ","explanation":"Code accesses credential files (SSH keys, AWS credentials, etc.). This could indicate credential theft attempts.","remediation":"Remove references to credential paths. Use environment variables or secrets managers. For docs, use placeholder paths (e.g., /path/to/config). Never load .env or token files in production code paths.","code_snippet":"    - $CWD/.cursorrules, $CWD/.windsurfrules, $CWD/.clinerules\n    - $CWD/CLAUDE.md, $CWD/copilot-instructions.md\n    - $CWD/.aider.conf.yml, $CWD/.continue/config.json\n    - $CWD/.env (env-scanner checks for leaked secrets — reads, never writes)\n  paths_write:\n    - ~/.shieldcortex/ (memory DB, config, cortex log, licence, audit cache)\n    - ~/.cache/shieldcortex/models (embedding model download cache)","intent":null,"tags":["Privilege Escalation","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{"llm_review_outcome":"disagreed","llm_review_confidence":0.93},"match_fingerprint":"66ef81c27c03406fd9935e5fc86fc4126d7150c15b8d076fdc528d05cea7c7bf","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":54,"end_line":null,"start_column":11}]},{"id":"AS2","finding_id":"finding-e4e042139a9845f1a8906215573cdb36","category":"Agent Snooping","pattern":"MCP Config Access","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":59,"end_line":null,"start_column":8},"finding":".claude/mcp.json","explanation":"Skill accesses MCP server configuration files (mcp.json). MCP configs contain server URLs, authentication tokens, and tool definitions — reading them allows the skill to discover and potentially abuse other tool integrations.","remediation":"Remove all code or instructions that read MCP configuration files (mcp.json). MCP server details should be managed by the agent runtime, not read by individual skills.","code_snippet":"    - ~/.shieldcortex/ (memory DB, config, cortex log, licence, audit cache)\n    - ~/.cache/shieldcortex/models (embedding model download cache)\n    - ~/.openclaw/extensions/shieldcortex-realtime/ (OpenClaw plugin via the wrapper install only; native `openclaw plugins install` uses OpenClaw's managed npm tree instead)\n    - ~/.claude/mcp.json, ~/.cursor/mcp.json (MCP server registration, when user runs setup)\n  network_endpoints:\n    - https://api.shieldcortex.ai (Cloud sync + audit telemetry — only when Cloud sync is enabled; licence validation — only when a licence key is activated, fired at CLI `license activate` and the dashboard's activation call (POST /api/license/activate), with no periodic or background re-check; sends the subscription id, works with Cloud sync off; never called when no key is configured)\n    - https://huggingface.co (embedding-model download — Xenova/all-MiniLM-L6-v2, ~90 MB, fetched into ~/.cache/shieldcortex/models by the MCP server's background preload at s","intent":null,"tags":["Agent Snooping","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{"llm_review_outcome":"disagreed","llm_review_confidence":0.94},"match_fingerprint":"13b92143329ed14dcc6306c67e05dc4ba1fa8cce8e7395bc763dcc5351d71f6f","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":59,"end_line":null,"start_column":8}]},{"id":"MP3","finding_id":"finding-d4bbca27fe10485e9c22961095d6160f","category":"Memory Poisoning","pattern":"Memory Manipulation","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.8,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":104,"end_line":null,"start_column":544},"finding":"delete your memory","explanation":"Skill manipulates agent memory, state, or stored context. Memory corruption can alter personality, override safety rules, or cause unpredictable behavior.","remediation":"Protect agent memory and state from modification by untrusted content. Use read-only memory for critical instructions and validate all state changes.","code_snippet":"d.** Per-memory and filtered bulk deletes go through a delete ACL (own-only) and are recorded in the audit ledger. Revoke-by-source (`forget --fromSource`, bulk-delete every memory from one source — for purging a poisoned agent) is **disabled by default** and only enabled by an out-of-band human action (`shieldcortex config --allow-revoke-by-source`); even then it is bounded by a trust-hierarchy ACL (you must own the source or out-rank it) and a per-call row cap. A compromised agent cannot mass-delete your memory.\n- **The bundled dashboard never renders RESTRICTED content.** The local visualization API and its WebSocket feed redact credential-class (`RESTRICTED`) memory content before it reaches the browser — the row stays visible (title/metadata) so you can manage it, but the secret is withheld (view full content via the CLI). Credential patterns in titles/metadata are masked too. This is a display-surface safeguard on top of the on-disk store; it does not weaken the firewall.\n- **No ","intent":null,"tags":["Memory Poisoning","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{"llm_review_outcome":"disagreed","llm_review_confidence":0.95},"match_fingerprint":"705c69a8d995fcd5fb844b434b246be62805f3426b6a01384f21cd766021acaf","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":104,"end_line":null,"start_column":544}]},{"id":"AS1","finding_id":"finding-fb4f772ddac94aa2925f1b1d535d8ba5","category":"Agent Snooping","pattern":"Agent Config Directory Access","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":112,"end_line":null,"start_column":155},"finding":"~/.claude/settings.json","explanation":"Skill reads from agent configuration directories (.claude/, .codex/, .gemini/). These directories may contain API keys, personal settings, and other credentials that the skill has no legitimate need to access.","remediation":"Remove all code or instructions that access agent configuration directories (.claude/, .codex/, .gemini/). If configuration values are needed, pass them explicitly as parameters or environment variables — never read the agent's own config files.","code_snippet":" dashboard X-Ray page, tarball download with `--deep`), URLs you pass to `env scan`, and webhooks you configure (memory events and Iron Dome operator notifications). The dashboard binds to localhost by default but may be explicitly exposed with `SHIELDCORTEX_HOST`; when exposed, the loopback session-token endpoint stays disabled. The worker binds to localhost.\n- **Bundled source code.** The OpenClaw plugin and cortex-memory handler are shipped in the package for inspection before use.\n- **Lifecycle event handlers.** ShieldCortex registers lifecycle handlers that auto-extract important context from conversations. These are registered in `~/.claude/settings.json` during setup and can be removed at any time. They run locally, never phone home.\n- **Proactive recall.** The UserPromptSubmit handler queries local memory on each prompt (<100ms) and surfaces relevant context. Fully local, configurable: `shieldcortex config --proactive-recall false`.\n\n### Automatic self-heal at gateway bootstrap","intent":null,"tags":["Agent Snooping","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{"llm_review_outcome":"disagreed","llm_review_confidence":0.92},"match_fingerprint":"5a1df888db5d4ec0b5b9acca20cfc27be4af48718ceb134b7edd155d53abdf2c","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":112,"end_line":null,"start_column":155}]},{"id":"AE1","finding_id":"finding-2285c13c5a75473bb94780d135d0c067","category":"analysis-evasion","pattern":"Incomplete referenced artifact analysis","severity":"HIGH","confidence":1,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":135,"end_line":null},"finding":"bundled/cortex-memory-hook/handler.ts (partial)","explanation":"Referenced artifact was not completely inspected","remediation":"Review the reported expression and analyzer's parsing limitation; correct the scanner if it misinterprets valid source, then rerun the scan. Keep required references; incomplete analysis is not proof of malicious evasion.","code_snippet":"(`HOOK.md`, `handler.ts`, `runtime.mjs`) there so the gateway loads it from","intent":null,"tags":["coverage","reference","target-disposition:partial"],"evidence":{"target_path":"bundled/cortex-memory-hook/handler.ts","target_disposition":"partial","reasons":[{"reason_code":"static_parse_limit","message":"A security-relevant expression exceeded a bounded static parser's span limit.","phase":"static","analyzers":["static_patterns_tool_misuse"]}]},"match_fingerprint":"a484af8981846f78d68c066624c03b954d9aba07b584782fe1cceaef73d7be32","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":135,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"AS1","finding_id":"finding-6c116c4e9a114f40b1d37a3d3a21207f","category":"Agent Snooping","pattern":"Agent Config Directory Access","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":146,"end_line":null,"start_column":25},"finding":"~/.claude/settings.json","explanation":"Skill reads from agent configuration directories (.claude/, .codex/, .gemini/). These directories may contain API keys, personal settings, and other credentials that the skill has no legitimate need to access.","remediation":"Remove all code or instructions that access agent configuration directories (.claude/, .codex/, .gemini/). If configuration values are needed, pass them explicitly as parameters or environment variables — never read the agent's own config files.","code_snippet":"\n**Scope limits:** the self-heal writes only inside `~/.openclaw/hooks/**` and\ndeletes only the two `~/.clawdbot` hook directories named above. It does not\nmodify `openclaw.json`, `~/.claude/settings.json`, MCP config, shell configs,\nor any other file; it makes no network calls; failures are swallowed so it can\nnever block agent startup.\n","intent":null,"tags":["Agent Snooping","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{"llm_review_outcome":"disagreed","llm_review_confidence":0.99},"match_fingerprint":"5a1df888db5d4ec0b5b9acca20cfc27be4af48718ceb134b7edd155d53abdf2c","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":146,"end_line":null,"start_column":25}]},{"id":"E4","finding_id":"finding-65bc3973eaf0409b969099b3a869fe0d","category":"Data Exfiltration","pattern":"Context Leakage","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.75,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":166,"end_line":null,"start_column":287},"finding":"capture conversation","explanation":"Code or instructions that leak agent conversation context to external services, potentially exposing sensitive user interactions.","remediation":"Remove any code that sends prompts, responses, or session data externally. Preserve user privacy; never exfiltrate conversation content.","code_snippet":"\n## Data handling, privacy & consent\n\nShieldCortex is **local-first**: memory, scanning, and audit run entirely on your machine — no account, no telemetry by default, and no network use beyond fetching the embedding model on first use when it is not cached (see **First-use model download** above). Because the tool can auto-capture conversation content, here is exactly what it reads, stores, and (only if you opt in) transmits.\n\n- **What it reads.** With the lifecycle handlers enabled (opt-in at setup), ShieldCortex reads your agent **session transcripts — both your prompts and the assistant's replies** — to auto-extract memorable context. PreCompact (before context compaction) reads the recent transcript; the SessionEnd and Stop handlers are **off by default**; the OpenClaw integration extracts from assistant output (the `cortex-memory` hook does this on `/new` and `/stop` when `openclawAutoMemory` is `true`); the hook's keyword-trigger path is not registered on core OpenClaw 2026.9.6, ","intent":null,"tags":["Data Exfiltration","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{"llm_review_outcome":"disagreed","llm_review_confidence":0.88},"match_fingerprint":"3ba683c0c93b322eae8d3c5d9429b5ed3486cc013cd83cfac1a51f62331ffc5a","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":166,"end_line":null,"start_column":287}]},{"id":"AS1","finding_id":"finding-55941326098445e2b72df0a92b4b7d0d","category":"Agent Snooping","pattern":"Agent Config Directory Access","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":170,"end_line":null,"start_column":566},"finding":"~/.claude/settings.json","explanation":"Skill reads from agent configuration directories (.claude/, .codex/, .gemini/). These directories may contain API keys, personal settings, and other credentials that the skill has no legitimate need to access.","remediation":"Remove all code or instructions that access agent configuration directories (.claude/, .codex/, .gemini/). If configuration values are needed, pass them explicitly as parameters or environment variables — never read the agent's own config files.","code_snippet":"d — passes the defence pipeline first; high-confidence credential patterns (49 patterns across 25 providers) and content classified RESTRICTED are **blocked or quarantined before storage**, not saved as live memory. This is a strong filter, not a guarantee: low-confidence or low-entropy secrets can still be stored. On sensitive work, **review what auto-memory captures** and disable auto-extraction (`shieldcortex config --openclaw-auto-memory false`; the Claude Code handlers can be removed from `~/.claude/settings.json`).\n- **Keyword triggers are dormant on OpenClaw.** The `cortex-memory` hook contains keyword auto-save code (e.g. \"remember this\", \"don't forget\"), but it is not registered on core OpenClaw 2026.9.6: the hook's `events` list has no `message` key, so saying a phrase saves nothing through the hook. The code captures the *nearby* text, which may include more than the phrase, is capped (auto-extracts never outrank explicit saves) and runs through the same credential/injection","intent":null,"tags":["Agent Snooping","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{"llm_review_outcome":"disagreed","llm_review_confidence":0.98},"match_fingerprint":"5a1df888db5d4ec0b5b9acca20cfc27be4af48718ceb134b7edd155d53abdf2c","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":170,"end_line":null,"start_column":566}]},{"id":"PE3","finding_id":"finding-2ea0e3f5de134a0abd5e09219c0fca8a","category":"Privilege Escalation","pattern":"Credential Access","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.8,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":183,"end_line":null,"start_column":15},"finding":"read SSH key","explanation":"Code accesses credential files (SSH keys, AWS credentials, etc.). This could indicate credential theft attempts.","remediation":"Remove references to credential paths. Use environment variables or secrets managers. For docs, use placeholder paths (e.g., /path/to/config). Never load .env or token files in production code paths.","code_snippet":"\n## What it does NOT do\n\n- Does **not** read SSH keys, AWS credentials, GPG keys, or /etc/ files\n- Does **not** send your data to external servers, with three narrow, user-initiated exceptions: Cloud sync when you enable it, the subscription id sent to the licence endpoint when you activate a licence key, and event payloads to webhooks you configure (memory-event and Iron Dome operator notifications). Its remaining outbound calls are downloads/fetches that carry only the request itself — never memory or conversation content: npm-registry update checks and X-Ray package lookups (the package name appears in the URL), the huggingface.co embedding-model download, and URLs you explicitly pass to `env scan`\n- Does **not** modify .bashrc, .zshrc, .profile, or shell configs\n- Does **not** use `eval` or dynamic code execution of any kind","intent":null,"tags":["Privilege Escalation","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{"llm_review_outcome":"disagreed","llm_review_confidence":0.99},"match_fingerprint":"fc8c3716b17e8429d208405d950bd99fa1650962940ff350100354ddd3701efe","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":183,"end_line":null,"start_column":15}]},{"id":"RA1","finding_id":"finding-f1083baaadff4542b152be740710de31","category":"Rogue Agent","pattern":"Self-Modification","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":267,"end_line":null,"start_column":35},"finding":"Self-update","explanation":"Skill modifies its own code, configuration, or behavior at runtime. Self-modification enables an agent to escalate privileges, disable safety constraints, or install persistent backdoors.","remediation":"Prevent the skill from modifying its own code, SKILL.md, or configuration files. Treat skill files as read-only at runtime.","code_snippet":"\n### Maintenance\n```bash\nshieldcortex update              # Self-update (npm package + OpenClaw plugin + skill)\nshieldcortex maintain --dry-run  # Preview storage/memory hygiene (plain `maintain` applies it)\n```\n","intent":null,"tags":["Rogue Agent","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{"llm_review_outcome":"disagreed","llm_review_confidence":0.93},"match_fingerprint":"bd002ac10f47a5ff8b5acbe18edb9cf06dba73d787e329e8585d8f7a24c528d9","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":267,"end_line":null,"start_column":35}]},{"id":"PE3","finding_id":"finding-9a62b3138fdf4ff29ea43065b74adcd1","category":"Privilege Escalation","pattern":"Credential Access","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.6,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":282,"end_line":null,"start_column":20},"finding":".env ","explanation":"Code accesses credential files (SSH keys, AWS credentials, etc.). This could indicate credential theft attempts.","remediation":"Remove references to credential paths. Use environment variables or secrets managers. For docs, use placeholder paths (e.g., /path/to/config). Never load .env or token files in production code paths.","code_snippet":"\n### `audit` checks:\n- **Memory files** — ~/.claude/projects/, ~/.cursor/memories/, ~/.windsurf/memories/\n- **Environment** — .env files for leaked credentials (read-only check, never writes)\n- **MCP configs** — ~/.claude/mcp.json, ~/.openclaw/mcp.json, ~/.cursor/mcp.json, project-level equivalents\n- **Rules files** — CLAUDE.md, .cursorrules, copilot-instructions.md for injection patterns\n","intent":null,"tags":["Privilege Escalation","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{"llm_review_outcome":"disagreed","llm_review_confidence":0.94},"match_fingerprint":"66ef81c27c03406fd9935e5fc86fc4126d7150c15b8d076fdc528d05cea7c7bf","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":282,"end_line":null,"start_column":20}]},{"id":"AS2","finding_id":"finding-f19f390b3cfe4789b37a7137bd724a29","category":"Agent Snooping","pattern":"MCP Config Access","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":283,"end_line":null,"start_column":22},"finding":".claude/mcp.json","explanation":"Skill accesses MCP server configuration files (mcp.json). MCP configs contain server URLs, authentication tokens, and tool definitions — reading them allows the skill to discover and potentially abuse other tool integrations.","remediation":"Remove all code or instructions that read MCP configuration files (mcp.json). MCP server details should be managed by the agent runtime, not read by individual skills.","code_snippet":"### `audit` checks:\n- **Memory files** — ~/.claude/projects/, ~/.cursor/memories/, ~/.windsurf/memories/\n- **Environment** — .env files for leaked credentials (read-only check, never writes)\n- **MCP configs** — ~/.claude/mcp.json, ~/.openclaw/mcp.json, ~/.cursor/mcp.json, project-level equivalents\n- **Rules files** — CLAUDE.md, .cursorrules, copilot-instructions.md for injection patterns\n\n## What Gets Uploaded to Cloud","intent":null,"tags":["Agent Snooping","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{"llm_review_outcome":"disagreed","llm_review_confidence":0.97},"match_fingerprint":"13b92143329ed14dcc6306c67e05dc4ba1fa8cce8e7395bc763dcc5351d71f6f","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":283,"end_line":null,"start_column":22}]},{"id":"SDI-4","finding_id":"finding-bb4f6f5111bd473badaf77883e633f33","category":"Excessive Agency","pattern":"The comment at L010–L014 claims high/critical results remain blocked, but the default log/warn branches allow them.","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.99,"location":{"file":"bundled/openclaw-plugin/interceptor.js","start_line":10,"end_line":28},"finding":"The comment at L010–L014 claims high/critical results remain blocked, but the default log/warn branches allow them.","explanation":"With the default configuration, pipeline BLOCK results map to critical severity and QUARANTINE results map to high severity, but the corresponding log and warn branches return without blocking the tool call. The deny failure policies apply only to pipeline errors or unavailable/failed approvals, contrary to the comment's claim that blocking is preserved. Although the independent X-Ray guard blocks some injection patterns, threats detected only by the pipeline can still enter persistent agent memory, making this a significant security-enforcement bypass.","remediation":"Enforce BLOCK and QUARANTINE decisions before entering any log/warn return path, or introduce an explicit deny action as the default for critical/high results. Keep failure handling separate from enforcement of successful pipeline decisions, update the misleading comment, and add tests proving that pipeline BLOCK/QUARANTINE results prevent tool execution even when the X-Ray guard permits the input.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{"llm_review_outcome":"confirmed","llm_review_confidence":0.99},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"bundled/openclaw-plugin/interceptor.js","start_line":10,"end_line":28}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-1b69d49be6754ec69bcb66db8c60baf4","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":"MCP server referenced without pinned version: 'npx -y shieldcortex'.","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.97,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":63,"end_line":null},"finding":"npx -y shieldcortex","explanation":"The documented fallback runs `npx -y shieldcortex` without an exact version, allowing package retrieval and execution without a package-install confirmation. A compromised publisher or malicious future release could execute with the agent user's filesystem privileges; disclosure of this behavior does not mitigate the supply-chain risk.","remediation":"Replace the fallback with an explicitly provisioned, version-pinned local executable. If runtime installation is necessary, require approval, pin an audited version, and verify package integrity through a controlled installation process.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{"llm_review_outcome":"confirmed","llm_review_confidence":0.97},"match_fingerprint":"eca81eb844dee57b23d913fb2494a60f82506f58a09d1aca585df4373eb49cec","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":63,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"EA2","finding_id":"finding-2c86560d6b664461995043f2b9eb4f7d","category":"Excessive Agency","pattern":"Autonomous Decision Making","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.75,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":102,"end_line":null,"start_column":276},"finding":"without asking","explanation":"Skill enables autonomous high-impact decisions without human-in-the-loop verification. Critical operations (destructive commands, financial transactions, data deletion) should require explicit user confirmation.","remediation":"Add human-in-the-loop confirmation for destructive, irreversible, or high-impact operations. Never auto-execute commands that modify files, send data, or alter system state.","code_snippet":"eneric MCP get a memory server / scanner the model may ignore — they are **not bound**. Tool-output firewall defaults to advisory. `shieldcortex doctor` and `shieldcortex lease` report bound / not-bound / unknown per plane.\n- **Setup is user-initiated, with one bounded exception.** Installing hooks, registering the MCP server, and migrating data are manual steps the user runs in their terminal, and bare `quickstart` / `setup` asks before each action; a named host, as in `setup claude`, is wired without asking. The npm postinstall script (disclosed in the trust table above) never adds integrations that weren't already present — on global installs it only prints instructions, checks the native binding, seeds default config on first install, and refreshes an existing OpenClaw hook/plugin install. The exception: the bundled cortex-memory hook performs a small automatic self-heal at gateway bootstrap, documented in full under **\"Automatic self-heal at gateway bootstrap\"** below.\n- **Setup m","intent":null,"tags":["Excessive Agency","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{"llm_review_outcome":"disagreed","llm_review_confidence":0.94},"match_fingerprint":"8dc77d3dce9ba1f2672e813265a1b1a0c8594866ef38a4e978bf4f4451795465","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":102,"end_line":null,"start_column":276}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-b46523b90d9040a19ac905397321abd8","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":"MCP server referenced without pinned version: 'npx -y shieldcortex'.","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.97,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":110,"end_line":null},"finding":"npx -y shieldcortex","explanation":"This passage describes the same unpinned `npx -y shieldcortex` fallback as the finding at line 63, rather than an independent execution path. Automatic retrieval of a mutable package version exposes the privileged integration to compromised or malicious package releases.","remediation":"Remove the automatic download fallback and fail with installation instructions when the approved local executable is absent. Provision an audited exact version with verified integrity.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{"llm_review_outcome":"confirmed","llm_review_confidence":0.97},"match_fingerprint":"eca81eb844dee57b23d913fb2494a60f82506f58a09d1aca585df4373eb49cec","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":110,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-72678653f30e434caf44f21891f27817","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":"MCP server referenced without pinned version: 'npx -y shieldcortex'.","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.97,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":172,"end_line":null},"finding":"npx -y shieldcortex","explanation":"This is another description of the same automatic, unpinned ShieldCortex fallback. Its placement in a local MCP bridge increases the consequences of package compromise because downloaded code runs in the user's environment with access to agent-related data.","remediation":"Configure the bridge to use an approved local executable pinned to an audited release. Disable runtime registry fallback and require explicit approval for dependency installation or upgrades.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{"llm_review_outcome":"confirmed","llm_review_confidence":0.97},"match_fingerprint":"eca81eb844dee57b23d913fb2494a60f82506f58a09d1aca585df4373eb49cec","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":172,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-f4fa951da4844c58a4291394d7bbb81b","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":"MCP server referenced without pinned version: 'npx mcporter'.","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.88,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":172,"end_line":null},"finding":"npx mcporter","explanation":"The integration is described as spawning `npx mcporter` without an exact version or a guaranteed locked local dependency. If npm resolves it from the registry, a compromised or unexpected release can execute locally; using an argv array prevents shell injection but not malicious package execution.","remediation":"Install mcporter as a locked, integrity-verified dependency and invoke its resolved local executable directly. Fail closed if that dependency is absent rather than allowing npx to fetch an unspecified version.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{"llm_review_outcome":"confirmed","llm_review_confidence":0.88},"match_fingerprint":"07ad7dbb108faff5f08ad28c72c389b355800d63c4efe5e49abb4fe7b4b7488e","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":172,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-eb1a618ae1aa479ea8b4d5f648a2de6e","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":"MCP server referenced without pinned version: 'npx mcporter'.","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.88,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":187,"end_line":null},"finding":"npx mcporter","explanation":"The `npx mcporter` reference repeats the potentially unpinned dependency execution documented at line 172. The absence of a shell does not establish package provenance or ensure that npm executes an audited version, although the actual resolution behavior cannot be verified from this Markdown file.","remediation":"Resolve and execute a preinstalled, lockfile-pinned mcporter binary with verified integrity. Prohibit implicit registry installation when the local dependency is missing.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{"llm_review_outcome":"confirmed","llm_review_confidence":0.88},"match_fingerprint":"07ad7dbb108faff5f08ad28c72c389b355800d63c4efe5e49abb4fe7b4b7488e","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":187,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"EA2","finding_id":"finding-fda5c30b6789484f8aea9e2c5289775e","category":"Excessive Agency","pattern":"Autonomous Decision Making","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.85,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":189,"end_line":null,"start_column":15},"finding":"auto-approve","explanation":"Skill enables autonomous high-impact decisions without human-in-the-loop verification. Critical operations (destructive commands, financial transactions, data deletion) should require explicit user confirmation.","remediation":"Add human-in-the-loop confirmation for destructive, irreversible, or high-impact operations. Never auto-execute commands that modify files, send data, or alter system state.","code_snippet":"argv-array, local-only children: `osascript` with fixed script lines (macOS folder picker) and ShieldCortex's own Node binary re-spawned for `xray --watch` background scans (hook and server helpers re-spawn `process.execPath` the same way, always with fixed local script paths). Sudo-aware home resolution validates the username, then runs `getent passwd <user>` as an argv-array — never through a shell, no tilde-eval. User-run CLI commands (setup, service, migrate, uninstall, audit, doctor, the npx-staleness warning) and corrupt-database recovery run fixed local admin tools (`npm`, `launchctl`, `systemctl`, `sqlite3`), some through a shell, parameterised only by local paths and usernames\n- Does **not** bypass, disable, or override any agent safety mechanisms\n- Does **not** auto-approve actions or skip verification prompts\n- Does **not** mine cryptocurrency, trade tokens, manage wallets, or initiate purchases\n- Does **not** make purchases, place orders, or move money on the user's behalf\n","intent":null,"tags":["Excessive Agency","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{"llm_review_outcome":"disagreed","llm_review_confidence":0.99},"match_fingerprint":"d136f35fbcfa4c6db41b45ba9d17d36e2634ea52685668d0ec094a066e0ff6b8","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":189,"end_line":null,"start_column":15}]},{"id":"EA2","finding_id":"finding-ccf68742c5f64f419225bdcc41c0a784","category":"Excessive Agency","pattern":"Autonomous Decision Making","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.85,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":189,"end_line":null,"start_column":39},"finding":"skip verification","explanation":"Skill enables autonomous high-impact decisions without human-in-the-loop verification. Critical operations (destructive commands, financial transactions, data deletion) should require explicit user confirmation.","remediation":"Add human-in-the-loop confirmation for destructive, irreversible, or high-impact operations. Never auto-execute commands that modify files, send data, or alter system state.","code_snippet":"argv-array, local-only children: `osascript` with fixed script lines (macOS folder picker) and ShieldCortex's own Node binary re-spawned for `xray --watch` background scans (hook and server helpers re-spawn `process.execPath` the same way, always with fixed local script paths). Sudo-aware home resolution validates the username, then runs `getent passwd <user>` as an argv-array — never through a shell, no tilde-eval. User-run CLI commands (setup, service, migrate, uninstall, audit, doctor, the npx-staleness warning) and corrupt-database recovery run fixed local admin tools (`npm`, `launchctl`, `systemctl`, `sqlite3`), some through a shell, parameterised only by local paths and usernames\n- Does **not** bypass, disable, or override any agent safety mechanisms\n- Does **not** auto-approve actions or skip verification prompts\n- Does **not** mine cryptocurrency, trade tokens, manage wallets, or initiate purchases\n- Does **not** make purchases, place orders, or move money on the user's behalf\n","intent":null,"tags":["Excessive Agency","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{"llm_review_outcome":"disagreed","llm_review_confidence":0.99},"match_fingerprint":"8db53b29ee2a947f415f92059d24849bcd6dd8e0dd6b2e1cd45dc449b8f679e4","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":189,"end_line":null,"start_column":39}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-1bd1faffc9f84e639604d3c951505f52","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":"MCP server referenced without pinned version: 'npx shieldcortex'.","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"bundled/cortex-memory-hook/HOOK.md","start_line":118,"end_line":null},"finding":"npx shieldcortex","explanation":"The disable-auto-memory command invokes an unpinned npm package through npx. If an appropriate local installation is unavailable, npx can retrieve and execute a registry version whose contents may change; a compromised release could execute code with the user's permissions and access transcripts or the shared memory database. This is a CLI supply-chain risk rather than evidence of a malicious MCP server.","remediation":"Use a vetted, exact package version, such as npx shieldcortex@<approved-version> config --openclaw-auto-memory false. Prefer a verified, preinstalled executable managed through a locked dependency workflow, and document the direct configuration-file edit as an alternative that requires no package execution.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{"llm_review_outcome":"confirmed","llm_review_confidence":0.93},"match_fingerprint":"03c6d87b3683b7c0d6518886b4942c54cb25f62d751dd3ea0820a32a3661e627","occurrences":[{"file":"bundled/cortex-memory-hook/HOOK.md","start_line":118,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-3f3383d9bbc741a781da2a09693def21","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":"MCP server referenced without pinned version: 'npx shieldcortex'.","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"bundled/cortex-memory-hook/HOOK.md","start_line":124,"end_line":null},"finding":"npx shieldcortex","explanation":"The enable-auto-memory command uses npx without specifying an exact ShieldCortex version, potentially resolving and executing a changing registry release when no suitable local installation exists. A compromised dependency could run with the user's privileges, with sensitive session context and persistent memories potentially accessible in this environment. The documented functionality appears legitimate, but it does not mitigate package-resolution risk.","remediation":"Pin the command to a reviewed exact version, such as npx shieldcortex@<approved-version> config --openclaw-auto-memory true. Prefer a verified local installation with locked dependencies, and require review before updating the approved version.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{"llm_review_outcome":"confirmed","llm_review_confidence":0.93},"match_fingerprint":"03c6d87b3683b7c0d6518886b4942c54cb25f62d751dd3ea0820a32a3661e627","occurrences":[{"file":"bundled/cortex-memory-hook/HOOK.md","start_line":124,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-05055266a22147c2bd95d0b3e08a7db1","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":"MCP server referenced without pinned version: 'npx -y shieldcortex'.","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.98,"location":{"file":"bundled/cortex-memory-hook/HOOK.md","start_line":140,"end_line":null},"finding":"npx -y shieldcortex","explanation":"The documented first-use installation runs npx -y shieldcortex without an exact version, allowing registry package code to be downloaded and executed without an installation confirmation prompt. A compromised release or dependency could execute with the user's permissions; the hook's access to session transcripts and shared persistent memory increases the potential confidentiality and integrity impact. The described memory-filtering defenses do not protect against malicious package execution.","remediation":"Replace automatic unpinned execution with an explicitly approved, exact-version installation. Verify package provenance and integrity, use a lockfile-backed installation where applicable, and require approval before initial installation or version changes rather than relying on npx -y.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{"llm_review_outcome":"confirmed","llm_review_confidence":0.98},"match_fingerprint":"eca81eb844dee57b23d913fb2494a60f82506f58a09d1aca585df4373eb49cec","occurrences":[{"file":"bundled/cortex-memory-hook/HOOK.md","start_line":140,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-05e479a75d6a4d6fa1cdc6cb532d1e73","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":"MCP server referenced without pinned version: 'npx -y shieldcortex'.","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.98,"location":{"file":"bundled/cortex-memory-hook/runtime.mjs","start_line":97,"end_line":null},"finding":"npx -y shieldcortex","explanation":"When no configured or global binary is available, the runtime selects `npx -y shieldcortex` and passes it to mcporter as the stdio server command. This permits automatic execution of an unpinned package release; a compromised upstream release could execute with the hook's privileges and access its memory payloads and other accessible local data. The fallback is conditional, which reduces exposure, but its unattended execution increases the supply-chain risk.","remediation":"Require a locally installed, reviewed ShieldCortex version and fail closed when it is unavailable. If automatic provisioning is necessary, install an exact reviewed version through a lockfile-backed process with integrity verification, then invoke its local executable rather than resolving an unversioned package at runtime.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16"],"evidence":{"llm_review_outcome":"confirmed","llm_review_confidence":0.98},"match_fingerprint":"eca81eb844dee57b23d913fb2494a60f82506f58a09d1aca585df4373eb49cec","occurrences":[{"file":"bundled/cortex-memory-hook/runtime.mjs","start_line":97,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-180b6b85ad0549ada5fa1bda5e094f80","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":"MCP server referenced without pinned version: 'npx -y shieldcortex'.","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.7,"location":{"file":"bundled/cortex-memory-hook/runtime.mjs","start_line":98,"end_line":null},"finding":"npx -y shieldcortex","explanation":"npx commands without a version suffix (e.g. @1.0.0) create a rug-pull risk if the upstream server is compromised and publishes a malicious update.","remediation":"Pin the version: npx @scope/server@1.2.3","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{"llm_review_outcome":"disagreed","llm_review_confidence":0.99},"match_fingerprint":"eca81eb844dee57b23d913fb2494a60f82506f58a09d1aca585df4373eb49cec","occurrences":[{"file":"bundled/cortex-memory-hook/runtime.mjs","start_line":98,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-fd5c19158e3941538865dbbb45c63b9b","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":"MCP server referenced without pinned version: 'npx fallback'.","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.7,"location":{"file":"bundled/cortex-memory-hook/runtime.mjs","start_line":113,"end_line":null},"finding":"npx fallback","explanation":"npx commands without a version suffix (e.g. @1.0.0) create a rug-pull risk if the upstream server is compromised and publishes a malicious update.","remediation":"Pin the version: npx @scope/server@1.2.3","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{"llm_review_outcome":"disagreed","llm_review_confidence":1},"match_fingerprint":"e76479f4d761a74aaa2022dfd38b394e4ae594c9d6f816dc51e2e06cf6cad725","occurrences":[{"file":"bundled/cortex-memory-hook/runtime.mjs","start_line":113,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SDI-4","finding_id":"finding-41f6f505c8804a47b10169fbce545e6c","category":"Excessive Agency","pattern":"The module claims all scanning is fire-and-forget, but its tool-call hook awaits threat gating and propagates blocking errors.","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.96,"location":{"file":"bundled/openclaw-plugin/index.js","start_line":646,"end_line":656},"finding":"The module claims all scanning is fire-and-forget, but its tool-call hook awaits threat gating and propagates blocking errors.","explanation":"The module documentation at L007 states that all scanning operations are fire-and-forget. In contrast, the before_tool_call hook awaits interceptor.handleToolCall(context) and deliberately rethrows ShieldCortex blocking errors, allowing the security check to delay or prevent tool execution rather than run only in the background.","remediation":"Update the module documentation to distinguish asynchronous advisory LLM-input scanning from synchronous, potentially blocking tool-call threat gating. Explicitly document the blocking behavior and its configuration.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{"llm_review_outcome":"disagreed","llm_review_confidence":0.98},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"bundled/openclaw-plugin/index.js","start_line":646,"end_line":656}]}],"suppressed_count":0,"suppressed":[],"metadata":{"has_executable_scripts":true,"skillspector_version":"2.12.0","llm_requested":true,"llm_available":tru